<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Florida Keys</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> Keys are a chain of coral islands curving south-west from the southern tip of Florida for some 200 kilometres to Key West. Before European contact they were inhabited by peoples linked to the Calusa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tequesta">Tequesta</a>, and in the 18th century the last Calusa survivors took refuge there before leaving for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>. They are now joined to the mainland by the Overseas Highway.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florida-keys.jpg" alt="Florida Keys" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shanbin Zhao · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:U.S._Route_1,_Florida_Keys.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
